    "post_stream": {
      "posts": [
        {
          "id": 1913486,
          "username": "markriplabs",
          "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/90db22/{size}.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-13T18:46:53.694Z",
          "cooked": "<p>I’m trying to understand how smaller brands handle wholesale orders when they’re not on Plus or don’t use a full B2B portal.</p>\n<p>From what I’ve read here, a lot of stockists still send orders by email, a PDF order form or even a photo of a handwritten list, and someone types them into Shopify as a draft order.</p>\n<p>If that’s you, I’d love to hear how it actually works day to day:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Roughly how many wholesale orders came in by email or PDF last month?</li>\n<li>Who enters them, and how long does one take?</li>\n<li>What goes wrong most often (SKU mix-ups, case vs unit quantities, PO numbers, prices)?</li>\n<li>What have you tried to make it easier, and did it stick?</li>\n</ol>\n<p>I’m researching this, not selling anything. I’ll post a summary of the answers back in this thread so everyone can compare setups.</p>",
          "post_number": 1,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 5,
          "updated_at": "2026-10-13T18:46:53.694Z",
