        {
          "id": 1913488,
          "username": "ShopifyWithShafi",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/shopifywithshafi/{size}/416939_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-13T18:55:03.948Z",
          "cooked": "<p>I would suggest a simple workflow for brands on regular Shopify plans: collect wholesale orders through a standardized form or spreadsheet, validate SKUs, case quantities, wholesale pricing, and PO numbers, then use the information to create draft orders in Shopify. For recurring orders, a small automation can handle product matching and draft order creation, leaving staff to review exceptions before sending invoices.</p>\n<p>The key is to standardize the incoming order data first. Automating inconsistent emails and PDFs without that step can create more errors instead of saving time. This approach can work without Shopify Plus or a full B2B portal, and it gives merchants a clear starting point before investing in a larger system.</p>",
          "post_number": 2,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 5,
          "updated_at": "2026-10-13T18:55:03.948Z",
          "reply_count": 0,
          "reply_to_post_number": null,
