        {
          "id": 1913627,
          "username": "Zeeshan6236",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/zeeshan6236/{size}/416004_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-14T05:59:25.008Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Hi <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/markriplabs\">@markriplabs</a> — I can’t share order numbers, but on a non-Plus plan the draft order screen covers a lot of it. Each line has a custom price field, so wholesale rates don’t need discount codes, and the PO can go in the order notes. For regulars, use Duplicate on an existing draft and just change quantities. What native Shopify won’t enforce is case packs, a customer can still order one unit, so it’s either variant names like Case of 12 or an app. Which part do you want compared across stores?</p>",
          "post_number": 4,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 5,
          "updated_at": "2026-10-14T05:59:25.008Z",
