        {
          "id": 1913652,
          "username": "ahsandoesntcare",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/ahsandoesntcare/{size}/415687_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-14T07:03:25.782Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Hi <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/markriplabs\">@markriplabs</a> — most of that manual pain is fixable inside draft orders rather than with a portal. In Orders &gt; Drafts, when you add a product you can type the SKU straight into the search, then edit the unit price on the line to the wholesale price. Case vs unit mix-ups usually come from the variant itself, so if a case of 12 is a separate variant with its own SKU, staff can’t pick the wrong one. Put the PO number in Notes or a custom attribute so it carries through to the invoice. It’s the cleanest place to start before automating anything.</p>",
